	(text "U1901 (TPS7A9101) takes power from ANA6. CMD_ANA5 drives Q1901; R1901 (100\nkOhm) pulls EN_ANA5 low when Q1901 is off. Enable this stage after ANA6 is\nstable. PGR_ANA5 is pulled to AON by R1902 (10 kOhm); qualify its status with\ninput availability."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 156.21 65.3 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.55 1.55)
				(thickness 0.15)
				(color 33 43 55 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "cae1fc88-b96b-4289-8b56-9e14934f893c")
	)
	(text "R1905 (0.05 Ohm) drops 50 mV/A after feedback: V(ANA5) = 5.00 V - I x 0.05\nOhm. R1906 (10 kOhm) bleeds the output. U1901 has internal current limiting,\nUVLO, thermal shutdown and active discharge. Its 1 A rating must cover ANA5\nloads and the downstream ANA3V3 stage."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 156.21 141 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.55 1.55)
				(thickness 0.15)
				(color 33 43 55 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d6563496-285d-4d54-a164-828588f68a9d")
	)
	(text "This is the first low-noise stage after the ANA6 switching preregulator. ANA5\nsupplies MIRA's 5 V analog domain and feeds the ANA3V3 regulator. The LDO\nreduces switching ripple reaching the matrix-drive and measurement circuits,\nhelping preserve DAC and ADC accuracy."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 156.21 45.44 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.55 1.55)
				(thickness 0.15)
				(color 33 43 55 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "ef5d4385-9c9f-4ac6-9701-54536d043262")
	)
